    {
      "id": "wrapped-in-whitespace-only-javascript-trims",
      "note": "A byte-order mark and a no-break space either side, which is what a descriptor pasted out of a document editor carries. `trim()` removes both, so the role parses. Before this case the four implementations had three answers: Rust and Python kept the mark and refused the role, and the C++ edition kept both.",
